1
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:12,233
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:40,133
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:43,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,500
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,733
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,767 --> 00:00:59,633
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:00,800
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,467
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:04,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:07,300
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:09,800
<i> Don't!</i>

12
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,200
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

13
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:16,800
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

14
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,300
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

15
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:22,133
[GLASS SHATTERING]

16
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:24,667
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

17
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:28,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

18
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:31,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:32,533 --> 00:01:35,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:36,367
[GUNSHOTS]

21
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:37,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

22
00:01:37,633 --> 00:01:39,200
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

23
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

24
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,667
<i> Why did you shoot him?!</i>

25
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:54,567
<i>Django! That wasn't part
of our deal!</i>

26
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:57,567
<i>We're not going to kill him.
We're just going to scare him.</i>

27
00:01:57,567 --> 00:01:59,267
<i>You betrayed me!
I'll never forget</i>

28
00:01:59,267 --> 00:02:00,767
<i>what you did to me.
If I see you here again,</i>

29
00:02:00,767 --> 00:02:02,400
<i> I will kill you!</i>

30
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,867
<i> I'll serve my sentence here.</i>

31
00:02:03,867 --> 00:02:05,900
<i> I didn't do anything wrong,</i>

32
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:07,367
<i> that I was falsely accused.</i>

33
00:02:10,233 --> 00:02:12,267
<i>We'll have one less
troublemaker in here.</i>

34
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:13,400
<i> You're free to go.</i>

35
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,500
<i> This is a hold up!</i>

36
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:16,600
<i> Gabo!</i>

37
00:02:17,367 --> 00:02:18,633
<i>Your crew with Django
is ruthless.</i>

38
00:02:18,633 --> 00:02:20,267
You'll even go after cold rice.

39
00:02:20,267 --> 00:02:21,700
I need backup on Joaquin Street!

40
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,500
<i> There's a holdup happening
on a bus!</i>

41
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:26,367
<i> This is the police! Stop!</i>

42
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,433
<i>I'm not the robber!
I'm the one who helped them!</i>

43
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:38,567
<i> Damn you, Gabo!</i>

44
00:02:42,867 --> 00:02:45,267
<i>He's not the robber!
He helped us!</i>

45
00:02:45,267 --> 00:02:48,233
<i> Poor thing! Help him!</i>

46
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:53,567
<i>You pervert!
You took advantage of me!</i>

47
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:55,500
Took advantage?<i>
</i> You're the one who kissed me!

48
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,633
<i> You took advantage of me!</i>

49
00:02:56,633 --> 00:02:58,167
You think you're all that, huh?

50
00:02:58,167 --> 00:02:59,467
<i> You're beautiful.</i>

51
00:03:00,567 --> 00:03:02,600
<i>- What's your name?
- You're unbelievable.</i>

52
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,400
You really had the guts<i>
</i> to ask my name.

53
00:03:08,167 --> 00:03:08,933
[MAX] Sam!

54
00:03:16,433 --> 00:03:18,467
Look, I'm leaving.

55
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:20,767
Take care of the robbers.

56
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:24,667
- [MAX] Sam! Sam!
- Hey!

57
00:03:24,667 --> 00:03:26,833
- Hold on! We're not done!
- [MAX] Are you alright?

58
00:03:26,833 --> 00:03:29,633
- [SAM] Yes. I'm fine.
- Miss! You guys look cute.

59
00:03:29,633 --> 00:03:32,500
How fortunate.

60
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,867
You truly are my lucky charm.

61
00:03:34,867 --> 00:03:36,133
[SMACK]

62
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,400
- They tried to rob us!
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

63
00:03:39,367 --> 00:03:41,800
No one got hurt,
except for the bad guys.

64
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,433
[POLICE] Step aside! Step aside!

65
00:03:43,433 --> 00:03:44,833
Are you alright?

66
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:46,700
- Huh?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

67
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:48,933
- [MAX] Are you sure?
- [SAM] Thanks for arriving.

68
00:03:48,933 --> 00:03:50,400
[MAX] Luckily you called
right away!

69
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:57,833
Men! Secure the perimeter!
Handcuff all suspects.

70
00:03:57,867 --> 00:04:00,200
Make sure of that.
Put them in the patrol car!

71
00:04:00,967 --> 00:04:02,700
- No one escapes, okay?
- Max! Max! Max!

72
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,300
What happened here?

73
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:08,867
NLEA got a call that
a robbery was happening.

74
00:04:08,867 --> 00:04:10,867
We responded right away,
but when we arrived,

75
00:04:10,867 --> 00:04:13,900
the real hero, NCIA agent
Samantha Jacinto--

76
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:17,700
She quickly took action,
and caught the robbers.

77
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:18,667
Estrella!

78
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,500
Here with us today
is the hero

79
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:24,300
who stopped the robbery
in the bus,

80
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:26,467
NCIA agent Sam Jacinto.

81
00:04:26,467 --> 00:04:29,267
What happened here, and how
did you stop the robbery?

82
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,433
I was driving earlier
when I noticed the bus.

83
00:04:32,433 --> 00:04:33,733
The driver
was driving recklessly,

84
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:35,733
so they might get
into an accident.

85
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:37,767
I approached it,
and saw it was a mess inside.

86
00:04:37,767 --> 00:04:39,000
Apparently, there was a robbery.

87
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,333
The robber took a shot at me,
so I just did the same.

88
00:04:41,333 --> 00:04:44,500
I cuffed them here,
but there was a man who helped.

89
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,933
He's the one
who protected the passengers.

90
00:04:45,933 --> 00:04:47,900
Where is he?
Can we interview him?

91
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:50,000
- He left.
- Oli, Oli!

92
00:04:50,867 --> 00:04:52,333
Let's look for details
on the bus

93
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:53,667
and from the passengers,
come on.

94
00:04:53,667 --> 00:04:55,367
- Thank you, thank you.
- [MAX] Okay.

95
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:57,400
Sure that's clear?

96
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:00,333
Sam?

97
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,733
Who's that man
you were talking to?

98
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,667
No one. Don't mind him.

99
00:05:09,433 --> 00:05:11,433
I'm going back to the office,
they're probably looking for me.

100
00:05:11,433 --> 00:05:12,567
Be careful, okay?

101
00:05:12,567 --> 00:05:14,467
- Thank you.
- You know how mommy is.

102
00:05:14,467 --> 00:05:15,833
Alright, I'll take care of this.

103
00:05:17,967 --> 00:05:19,633
Estrella, make sure
everyone's safe.

104
00:05:19,633 --> 00:05:20,633
[ESTRELLA] Yes, ma'am.

105
00:05:20,633 --> 00:05:21,733
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

106
00:05:23,933 --> 00:05:26,433
[TOWN CRIER]<i> Calling
</i> all neighbors!

107
00:05:26,433 --> 00:05:29,567
<i> This is our chance!</i>

108
00:05:29,567 --> 00:05:32,567
<i>It is time for us
to take action!</i>

109
00:05:32,567 --> 00:05:34,767
<i> Stop idling around!</i>

110
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,467
<i> And you!</i>

111
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:38,433
<i> Stop giving them money!</i>

112
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:40,500
How will we earn their respect?

113
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:43,500
Nothing good comes from gossip.

114
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:46,500
<i>Mind your own business
and work on yourselves!</i>

115
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:49,733
<i> Stop relying on luck!</i>

116
00:05:49,733 --> 00:05:52,600
<i>Success won't just fall
into your lap.</i>

117
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:55,767
<i>What else are you
waiting for, neighbors?</i>

118
00:05:56,433 --> 00:05:58,433
<i> Let's take action!</i>

119
00:06:09,867 --> 00:06:11,133
I'm back

120
00:06:11,833 --> 00:06:13,333
where I belong!

121
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:21,667
[OVERLAPPING CHATTERING]

122
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,500
How's it going?

123
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:28,800
Hey!

124
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:32,433
[WOMAN 1] Pedring,
you're out here drinking again!

125
00:06:32,433 --> 00:06:35,367
You useless bastard!

126
00:06:35,367 --> 00:06:37,167
I'll drag you back
to your mother!

127
00:06:37,167 --> 00:06:38,967
[WOMAN 2] Come and buy one!

128
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:43,833
Come and buy one!

129
00:06:44,033 --> 00:06:45,200
Come and get<i> pagpag
</i>(scavenged leftovers)!

130
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:47,833
<i> Pagpag</i> (scavenged leftovers)!
Come get it here!

131
00:06:49,467 --> 00:06:50,833
- Miss!
- Come buy here!

132
00:06:50,833 --> 00:06:53,700
- My favorite! How much is this?
- One hundred.

133
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:55,867
This used to be thirty!
Why did the price go up?

134
00:06:55,867 --> 00:06:59,367
[WOMAN 2] Prices have
increased since the war.

135
00:06:59,867 --> 00:07:01,533
- [WOMAN 2] Thank you.
- No problem.

136
00:07:01,533 --> 00:07:02,633
Hmm. [SMOOCHES]

137
00:07:02,633 --> 00:07:04,533
My favorite! [CHUCKLES]

138
00:07:04,533 --> 00:07:06,700
[WOMAN 2] Come and get yours!

139
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:07,700
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

140
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:14,667
[CROWD CHEERING]

141
00:07:16,867 --> 00:07:18,567
<i> Our girl just scored a point!</i>

142
00:07:18,567 --> 00:07:20,433
Just like the person next to me,

143
00:07:20,433 --> 00:07:23,100
<i>- she scored big!
- C'mon, girl!</i>

144
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:26,233
[CROWD CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

145
00:07:26,233 --> 00:07:27,567
They'll lose! That's nothing!

146
00:07:28,233 --> 00:07:33,167
[INAUDIBLE]

147
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:36,500
[CROWD CHEERING]

148
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:40,200
<i> Team Emeruit is leading!</i>

149
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:47,200
[CROWD CHEERING]

150
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:54,700
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,467
- Gosh!
- Team Emeruit--

152
00:07:59,467 --> 00:08:01,733
- It's Gabo!
- It's Gabo!

153
00:08:02,067 --> 00:08:03,567
It's Gabo!

154
00:08:03,567 --> 00:08:05,267
It's Gabo!

155
00:08:05,267 --> 00:08:07,033
- It's Gabo!
- It's Gabo!

156
00:08:08,767 --> 00:08:11,100
[WOMAN 1] Gabo!
Your hair is so long!

157
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,733
You're here!

158
00:08:13,467 --> 00:08:14,800
Gabo!

159
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,033
[WOMAN 2] Look, it's Gabo!

160
00:08:16,033 --> 00:08:18,067
- Look, it's Gabo!
- Tekla!

161
00:08:18,767 --> 00:08:21,600
- Tekla! Tekla!
- [CROWD SCREAMING]

162
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:23,100
Where's my grandchild?!

163
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,933
What's going on?

164
00:08:25,933 --> 00:08:28,067
- Gabo is out!
- It's Gabo!

165
00:08:28,067 --> 00:08:30,467
[SCREAMING]

166
00:08:31,133 --> 00:08:33,967
[SQUEALING] Gabo! Gabo!

167
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,500
Step aside! Gabo!

168
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,900
[SQUEALING] Gabo!

169
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:43,633
[CROWD CHEEERING]

170
00:08:43,633 --> 00:08:44,967
[SMOOCHING]

171
00:08:44,967 --> 00:08:46,500
Gabo, I've missed you!

172
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,633
Why didn't you
tell me you were going home?

173
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:49,667
Tekla?

174
00:08:49,667 --> 00:08:51,100
Yes, it's me!

175
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,833
- [MAN] Hey!
- Ouch! Hey, it hurts!

176
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:55,167
Hey, what's going on?

177
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,433
Step aside!

178
00:08:56,433 --> 00:08:59,100
He doesn't like you
because you're all ugly!

179
00:09:00,833 --> 00:09:02,933
They're attacking
my granddaughter!

180
00:09:03,533 --> 00:09:06,100
Nobody is interested
in people like you!

181
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:08,300
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- Hey! Stop that!

182
00:09:09,967 --> 00:09:11,733
- You're ugly! Ugly!
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

183
00:09:13,133 --> 00:09:15,567
That's enough! Enough!

184
00:09:17,667 --> 00:09:20,100
[TEKLA] C'mon,
I'll bring you back to my place!

185
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,767
I mean... back to your place.

186
00:09:22,167 --> 00:09:24,700
[IBYANG] What's this?
Why did you only make this much?

187
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:28,633
We can't afford to slow down,
or we'll lose our customers!

188
00:09:28,667 --> 00:09:31,300
What's going on here!
Hurry up!

189
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:33,033
Wash those properly!

190
00:09:33,033 --> 00:09:34,833
You can start using this.

191
00:09:34,833 --> 00:09:37,567
Don't fill it up too much,
I'll lose money!

192
00:09:37,567 --> 00:09:39,367
Seal it properly
so it looks legit.

193
00:09:39,367 --> 00:09:40,967
Start moving!

194
00:09:40,967 --> 00:09:42,133
Hey, you..

195
00:09:42,133 --> 00:09:45,200
Make sure to charge extra
on the buses you ride, okay?

196
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,700
Go, hurry!

197
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:48,333
[MAN] I'll teach you, okay?

198
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,167
Do you see this gun?

199
00:09:51,167 --> 00:09:53,733
This isn't a toy,
this is a deadly weapon!

200
00:09:53,733 --> 00:09:55,033
Do you understand?

201
00:09:55,033 --> 00:09:56,700
- [CHILDREN] Yes, sir!
- Alright, run along!

202
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:58,167
Yes, sir!

203
00:10:01,367 --> 00:10:02,867
Where's the boss?

204
00:10:02,867 --> 00:10:04,233
He's right there.

205
00:10:04,233 --> 00:10:10,367
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

206
00:10:13,667 --> 00:10:15,900
Hey, why are you here?

207
00:10:17,267 --> 00:10:19,300
- What's wrong?
- We need some money.

208
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,600
Come on.

209
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:29,567
[CURIOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

210
00:10:33,233 --> 00:10:34,800
[IBYANG] Django!

211
00:10:39,133 --> 00:10:40,267
What is it?

212
00:10:40,267 --> 00:10:42,133
These kids are looking for you.

213
00:10:42,133 --> 00:10:43,867
[IBYANG] Marites,
why don't you come with me?

214
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:47,133
Clean up there, too.

215
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:49,100
Boss, here's all
the money we made.

216
00:10:49,867 --> 00:10:51,400
- Pa.
- Hmm?

217
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,267
What's going on?

218
00:10:53,267 --> 00:10:54,900
Oh.

219
00:10:57,967 --> 00:10:59,767
Would you look at that!

220
00:10:59,767 --> 00:11:01,733
You've already hit
your quota in just one week!

221
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,900
- For real?
- These kids of yours

222
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:05,100
are just built different!

223
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:06,367
Of course!

224
00:11:06,367 --> 00:11:09,033
They can get out right away
since they're still kids, eh?

225
00:11:09,067 --> 00:11:10,733
So just keep at it! [SMACKS]

226
00:11:10,733 --> 00:11:14,100
Obviously. And don't lump us in
with Topak. That flop.

227
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:16,067
Why? What happened with Topak?

228
00:11:16,067 --> 00:11:17,267
Cops caught them.

229
00:11:17,267 --> 00:11:20,667
What now, Pops? Topak rakes in
quite a good amount, too.

230
00:11:20,667 --> 00:11:22,100
Just let him stay there for now.

231
00:11:22,433 --> 00:11:24,267
Take a short vacation inside.

232
00:11:24,833 --> 00:11:26,300
Once the weather cools down,

233
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:28,267
then we'll get them out.

234
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:29,133
Hmm.

235
00:11:29,133 --> 00:11:31,200
Right, then. Go and grab a bite,
boys.

236
00:11:31,433 --> 00:11:33,000
- Hey.
- What?

237
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,433
[IBYANG] We struck it big, eh?

238
00:11:37,967 --> 00:11:39,067
[INAUDIBLE]

239
00:11:39,067 --> 00:11:41,000
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

240
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,733
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:11:44,767 --> 00:11:46,000
[TIRES SCREECH]

242
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,067
[HANDBRAKE CLICKS]

243
00:11:49,133 --> 00:11:50,133
[THUDS]

244
00:12:01,333 --> 00:12:02,800
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

245
00:12:05,333 --> 00:12:06,500
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

246
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:10,200
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:14,767
[AVELINO]<i> At least 30 bus
</i> passengers made it safe

248
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:19,133
from a robbery by a group of men
<i> at Joaquin Street in Manila.</i>

249
00:12:19,133 --> 00:12:21,033
<i> Agent Samantha Jacinto</i>

250
00:12:21,033 --> 00:12:25,167
<i>of the National Criminal
Investigation Agency or NCIA,</i>

251
00:12:25,167 --> 00:12:27,167
<i>- saved the victims.
- Good morning, Ma'am Jacinto!</i>

252
00:12:27,167 --> 00:12:29,733
[SALVADOR]<i> The hero who stopped
</i> the robbery in the bus,

253
00:12:29,733 --> 00:12:31,867
<i>- NCIA Agent Sam Jacinto.
- Look at you go!</i>

254
00:12:31,867 --> 00:12:33,367
<i>According to Jacinto,
she noticed the bus</i>

255
00:12:33,367 --> 00:12:34,733
<i> running in a strange manner.</i>

256
00:12:34,733 --> 00:12:37,233
When she approached the vehicle,
<i> she saw the criminals inside.</i>

257
00:12:37,233 --> 00:12:41,067
<i>However, one man helped her
in fighting</i>

258
00:12:41,067 --> 00:12:42,900
<i>- said criminals.
- Great job, ma'am!</i>

259
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:44,133
Had you not been there

260
00:12:44,133 --> 00:12:46,200
that group would've succeeded
again!

261
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,200
I just did what I had to do.

262
00:12:48,233 --> 00:12:49,533
Wow!

263
00:12:49,533 --> 00:12:52,067
- Wow, congrats!
- [ALL APPLAUDING]

264
00:12:52,067 --> 00:12:54,100
We know it's your job,
Ma'am Jacinto.

265
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:55,400
But it still made us proud.

266
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,900
Good thing you beat them
even with just yourself!

267
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:59,333
Amazing! Badass!

268
00:12:59,333 --> 00:13:01,000
Hey, watch your mouth!

269
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,533
What, you think Ma'am Sam
is incapable of doing so?

270
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:06,233
That's not it. We all know
we're very capable.

271
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:08,567
It just so happens
that it's Ma'am Jacinto's day.

272
00:13:08,567 --> 00:13:11,233
Really? Spare me the flattery.

273
00:13:11,233 --> 00:13:13,400
- Get back to your job.
- [LAUGHING]

274
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,900
- Amazing!
- Congrats!

275
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,333
- You were great!
- Congratulations!

276
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:18,200
Alright!

277
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:20,367
[AGENT 1] Ma'am, congrats!

278
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,100
[SAM] Thanks.

279
00:13:22,133 --> 00:13:23,400
[AGENT 2] Good morning, ma'am!

280
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:26,200
- Ma'am, congrats!
- [AGENT 3] Congrats, ma'am!

281
00:13:27,233 --> 00:13:28,567
Huh? What's this?

282
00:13:28,567 --> 00:13:30,000
[KAREN] Wow!

283
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,933
- [FOLDER THUDS]
- Who sent this?

284
00:13:32,267 --> 00:13:35,000
Why are you asking as if
you're not an investigator?

285
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:36,233
Sam.

286
00:13:37,567 --> 00:13:39,400
How is it? Did you like it?

287
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:42,233
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

288
00:13:42,233 --> 00:13:43,267
Mmm.

289
00:13:43,267 --> 00:13:44,533
What's this for, sir?

290
00:13:44,967 --> 00:13:46,100
I'm not sure.

291
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,333
What do you think?

292
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:50,200
Um...

293
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:51,533
It could be because...

294
00:13:52,533 --> 00:13:54,233
I want to congratulate you

295
00:13:54,233 --> 00:13:56,300
for saving those people.

296
00:13:56,333 --> 00:13:58,067
Or it could also be because...

297
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:00,867
I'm still waiting for...

298
00:14:01,333 --> 00:14:03,167
- you to say yes.
- [RALLOS] Oh!

299
00:14:03,167 --> 00:14:05,933
My idol is truly
a smooth operator!

300
00:14:07,933 --> 00:14:10,967
Ma'am Sam, can't you even say
a little thank you

301
00:14:10,967 --> 00:14:12,800
for this sweet gesture?

302
00:14:13,067 --> 00:14:14,033
Mm.

303
00:14:14,967 --> 00:14:16,433
Thank you. Thank you, sir.

304
00:14:17,067 --> 00:14:18,133
Excuse me.

305
00:14:18,567 --> 00:14:19,567
[BOUQUET THUDS]

306
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:20,867
[CHAIR RATTLING]

307
00:14:21,833 --> 00:14:23,367
- [CHAIR RATTLES]
- [THUDS]

308
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:26,233
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

309
00:14:26,233 --> 00:14:27,433
[INHALES SHARPLY]

310
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:28,533
Sam.

311
00:14:29,167 --> 00:14:31,600
Is there something wrong?
Are you okay?

312
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,133
- Mm.
- [KAREN] Oh.

313
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:36,033
I know you like the back
of my hand.

314
00:14:36,033 --> 00:14:37,333
There is.

315
00:14:37,333 --> 00:14:39,333
It's not like you're allergic
to flowers.

316
00:14:39,333 --> 00:14:42,600
[QUIRKY STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

317
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:44,133
There's just...

318
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,500
something that happened
during the incident.

319
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:47,500
What?!

320
00:14:47,933 --> 00:14:49,133
What happened?!

321
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,367
There was...

322
00:14:53,367 --> 00:14:55,500
a man who attempted to kiss me.

323
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,167
- [THUDS]
- That bastard!

324
00:14:57,167 --> 00:14:58,867
Why did he kiss you?!

325
00:14:58,867 --> 00:15:00,967
Is he one of the suspects?
A victim?

326
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,133
No.

327
00:15:02,133 --> 00:15:05,167
I don't know why he's there
or even who-- who he is.

328
00:15:05,167 --> 00:15:06,533
Who's that bastard?

329
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,333
Did you get his name?

330
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:10,533
Bring his ass to me!
I'll beat him up!

331
00:15:10,533 --> 00:15:11,467
I won't spare him!

332
00:15:11,467 --> 00:15:14,367
Wow. That random guy
beat you to it.

333
00:15:14,367 --> 00:15:15,300
Exactly!

334
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:17,500
Can you all please stop
this nonsense?

335
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,200
You guys are so embarrassing,
you're too loud--

336
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,400
Sam, you don't deserve
to be disrespected like that!

337
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,700
Now, tell me who that man is!

338
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:26,467
Bring hiss ass to me! I'll beat
him up! I won't spare him!

339
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:27,700
I told you, enough!

340
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:29,367
I'm the one who got wronged

341
00:15:29,367 --> 00:15:30,967
so I'm the one
who'll deal with it.

342
00:15:30,967 --> 00:15:32,667
Once I find out who he is
I'll be the one to throw him

343
00:15:32,667 --> 00:15:34,167
to jail and not you!

344
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:35,700
[SEBASTIAN SIGHS]

345
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,433
[KAREN] Oh, wow...

346
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:42,567
He's still courting her but he
already cares for her a lot.

347
00:15:43,167 --> 00:15:44,400
Won't you just go out
with him already, ma'am?

348
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:46,400
I mean, you look good
together anyway.

349
00:15:48,167 --> 00:15:49,367
[CASTOR] Team, let's go!

350
00:15:49,367 --> 00:15:51,233
Sir Delgado is calling us.

351
00:15:52,933 --> 00:15:55,167
- Let's go.
- Sam, come on.

352
00:15:59,367 --> 00:16:05,733
[QUIRKY STIRRING MUSIC
CONTINUES]

353
00:16:05,733 --> 00:16:06,967
[THUDS]

354
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:15,933
Jacinto.

355
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,000
[SAM] Sir.

356
00:16:18,533 --> 00:16:19,767
Good job!

357
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:26,033
[DJANGO] You sure about this?

358
00:16:26,033 --> 00:16:27,933
[MAN] We've been watching
them for days.

359
00:16:27,933 --> 00:16:29,767
The owner leaves
at nine o'clock.

360
00:16:29,767 --> 00:16:31,267
[DJANGO] How many stay behind?

361
00:16:31,267 --> 00:16:32,400
[MAN] Two.

362
00:16:32,733 --> 00:16:34,233
The wife and the maid.

363
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:35,333
Alright.

364
00:16:36,467 --> 00:16:37,800
Wait until the man leaves.

365
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,367
We'll go in through the back.

366
00:16:39,367 --> 00:16:41,233
Take everything.

367
00:16:41,233 --> 00:16:42,467
It's all set, Django.

368
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,867
Alright, we're heading out.

369
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,733
[ROMY] Django!

370
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:49,300
This is Tuklaw.

371
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,367
He said he's got a job for us.

372
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:55,900
You guys handle that.

373
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:57,300
I'm heading out.

374
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:06,933
Right now?

375
00:17:07,667 --> 00:17:09,533
- What's the job?
- We've got a hit.

376
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:12,333
A construction company owner
in Batangas.

377
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:13,900
The details are in the envelope.

378
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:15,633
How much?

379
00:17:15,667 --> 00:17:16,867
Fifty thousand.

380
00:17:16,867 --> 00:17:18,867
Half up front.

381
00:17:18,867 --> 00:17:21,700
Once the job's done,
another fifty.

382
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:22,767
Full payment.

383
00:17:23,467 --> 00:17:24,600
[CHUCKLES]

384
00:17:25,367 --> 00:17:26,867
Damn it...

385
00:17:26,867 --> 00:17:28,800
We've got a job in Camarin.

386
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,967
What are we supposed to do?

387
00:17:31,433 --> 00:17:32,633
Django...

388
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:35,867
Your Uncle Romy and I
can handle this.

389
00:17:35,867 --> 00:17:37,500
You sure, Pa? Can you manage?

390
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:38,600
[SCOFFS]

391
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:40,567
What do you take us for,
rookies?

392
00:17:40,867 --> 00:17:42,233
[CHUCKLES]

393
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,600
Hey, Romy.

394
00:17:45,333 --> 00:17:46,667
Get the guns ready.

395
00:17:46,667 --> 00:17:48,533
It's always ready.

396
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:50,267
Always well-oiled so...

397
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,700
- [PAQUITO SCOFFS]
- [ROMY] Come on.

398
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,433
[MAN] Give me the ball!
Pass it!

399
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:03,800
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

400
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:05,567
- [KEYBOARD CLICKING]
- Hurry up!

401
00:18:05,567 --> 00:18:08,567
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

402
00:18:08,567 --> 00:18:10,433
[DABOY] A tough guy, huh?

403
00:18:11,667 --> 00:18:14,433
[METAL SCREWING]

404
00:18:18,567 --> 00:18:21,500
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:18:23,033 --> 00:18:24,100
Ma...

406
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,767
Ma, the water bill just arrived.

407
00:18:25,767 --> 00:18:27,767
Pay it. It's only
two hundred pesos anyway.

408
00:18:27,767 --> 00:18:29,333
Ma, it's not two hundred!

409
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:30,700
The bill is eight thousand!

410
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:32,367
What?
Why is it eight thousand?

411
00:18:32,367 --> 00:18:34,033
Do we have a swimming pool
or something?

412
00:18:34,033 --> 00:18:35,933
I don't know why
it's eight thousand...

413
00:18:35,933 --> 00:18:37,067
- Kulas!
- What?

414
00:18:37,067 --> 00:18:38,767
- Come look at this!
- Look, Pa.

415
00:18:38,767 --> 00:18:40,433
It's eight thousand.

416
00:18:40,433 --> 00:18:42,033
Yeah, it's eight thousand.

417
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:43,867
How could it possibly be
eight thousand?

418
00:18:43,867 --> 00:18:44,967
Look over there!

419
00:18:47,033 --> 00:18:48,933
Get the crowbar and the shovel.

420
00:18:48,933 --> 00:18:50,467
- Hurry!
- Okay, Pa.

421
00:18:50,833 --> 00:18:52,067
[DIDAY] Hurry up!

422
00:18:53,533 --> 00:18:54,833
[ESTONG] Ma, move aside.

423
00:18:54,867 --> 00:18:58,000
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

424
00:18:58,867 --> 00:19:00,400
[DIDAY] Go on, dig it up!

425
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:02,367
There could be a lot
of pipes connected to it!

426
00:19:02,367 --> 00:19:06,367
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

427
00:19:06,367 --> 00:19:08,633
[KULAS] Diday!
No wonder our bill's so high.

428
00:19:08,633 --> 00:19:10,467
So many people are tapped
into our water line.

429
00:19:10,467 --> 00:19:11,533
See? I told you.

430
00:19:11,533 --> 00:19:13,633
You've all got some nerve!
Where's my machete?

431
00:19:13,633 --> 00:19:14,767
[ESTONG] Ma!

432
00:19:14,767 --> 00:19:16,400
Don't get too worked up!

433
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,800
Pa, stop her!

434
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:19,467
- Ma!
- [KULAS] Come on!

435
00:19:19,467 --> 00:19:20,633
[ESTONG] Ma!

436
00:19:20,633 --> 00:19:21,800
Ma!

437
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,433
- [DIDAY YELLING]
- [ESTONG] Ma!

438
00:19:23,433 --> 00:19:24,733
Here comes Miss Diday again.

439
00:19:24,933 --> 00:19:26,533
[DIDAY] You people are
unbelievable!

440
00:19:26,533 --> 00:19:28,600
- Here comes another fight.
- [LAUGHS]

441
00:19:28,633 --> 00:19:30,667
- You'll pay for this, okay?
- I got it!

442
00:19:30,667 --> 00:19:32,967
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

443
00:19:32,967 --> 00:19:34,467
[METAL SCREWING]

444
00:19:34,467 --> 00:19:36,933
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

445
00:19:36,933 --> 00:19:38,667
- [CHUCKLING]
- Wave it around!

446
00:19:38,667 --> 00:19:39,967
Maybe you'll hit somebody!

447
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,967
- Hey, stop her!
- Go on, slash them!

448
00:19:43,667 --> 00:19:44,967
- Run!
- Hey!

449
00:19:45,833 --> 00:19:46,900
Rudy!

450
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:48,933
[WOMAN] Diday, you might
actually hit someone!

451
00:19:48,933 --> 00:19:50,933
- What's going on?
- Diday's losing it again!

452
00:19:50,933 --> 00:19:52,800
- I wonder why.
- Look at her!

453
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,633
How am I supposed to pay
eight thousand?

454
00:19:54,633 --> 00:19:55,800
What's going on?

455
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,900
- What's Diday doing?
- Who knows?

456
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:59,600
She just suddenly went crazy.

457
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:00,833
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

458
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:02,833
Diday, you might hit someone
with that!

459
00:20:02,867 --> 00:20:04,033
Hey, Diday!

460
00:20:04,033 --> 00:20:05,833
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

461
00:20:05,833 --> 00:20:07,633
- Hey!
- She's carrying a machete!

462
00:20:07,633 --> 00:20:08,667
Stop that!

463
00:20:10,633 --> 00:20:12,533
I barely recognized you, Tekla.

464
00:20:12,533 --> 00:20:15,167
- You've really grown up.
- I'm even prettier now, right?

465
00:20:15,167 --> 00:20:17,700
That's why those gays
are so jealous of me.

466
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,667
I was wondering who
they were arguing with.

467
00:20:19,667 --> 00:20:20,800
[TEKLA CHUCKLES]

468
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,833
No wonder they're
so annoyed with you.

469
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:25,000
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

470
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,133
What's going on?

471
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:27,633
[TEKLA] There.

472
00:20:27,633 --> 00:20:29,433
Miss Diday's throwing a fit
again.

473
00:20:29,433 --> 00:20:31,500
She probably found out that
everyone around here

474
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,467
is tapped into their water line.

475
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,200
Gabo?

476
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:38,967
Gabo!

477
00:20:38,967 --> 00:20:40,167
- Gabo!
- Pa!

478
00:20:40,167 --> 00:20:41,233
Pa!

479
00:20:41,233 --> 00:20:42,533
- Gabo!
- Pa!

480
00:20:42,533 --> 00:20:44,633
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

481
00:20:44,633 --> 00:20:45,800
- Pa!
- [DANTE] Gabo!

482
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:46,867
Gabo!

483
00:20:46,867 --> 00:20:47,900
[GABO] Pa!

484
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:50,233
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

485
00:20:50,233 --> 00:20:52,000
It's Gabo! He's here!

486
00:20:52,833 --> 00:20:54,800
- Oh!
- [DANTE] Gabo!

487
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,067
- Gabo!
- Aunty!

488
00:20:56,067 --> 00:20:57,633
Thank God!

489
00:20:57,967 --> 00:21:00,167
Tolits, Django needs
to know about this.

490
00:21:00,167 --> 00:21:01,400
He won't last long here.

491
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,167
Django's going to come
after him right away.

492
00:21:03,167 --> 00:21:05,133
- [CRYING] He's here.
- Hey.

493
00:21:05,133 --> 00:21:06,733
- Gabo.
- Miss Betchay.

494
00:21:06,733 --> 00:21:09,667
So you're finally home.
You didn't even tell us.

495
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:10,967
What should we do?

496
00:21:11,767 --> 00:21:13,667
Come on!
Let's tell Django!

497
00:21:13,667 --> 00:21:14,933
Let's go!

498
00:21:14,933 --> 00:21:17,033
Nice entrance. You look like
you just got back from Saudi.

499
00:21:17,033 --> 00:21:18,600
[LAUGHS]

500
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:19,567
Wow, Gabo!

501
00:21:19,567 --> 00:21:21,267
- You've really changed.
- [DANTE] Yeah.

502
00:21:21,267 --> 00:21:23,200
You look like a movie star.

503
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,033
[IPE] Gabo! Good thing
you're finally out.

504
00:21:26,033 --> 00:21:28,767
We thought you'd be stuck
in there for a long time.

505
00:21:28,767 --> 00:21:30,000
[BONG] What happened?

506
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,767
You bastard.
I thought you'd rot in there.

507
00:21:31,767 --> 00:21:33,200
[MAMENG] Look at this guy!

508
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,567
Gabo, how'd you get out?

509
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,100
Were you released...

510
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:40,867
...or did you escape?

511
00:21:40,867 --> 00:21:42,033
- Uh, Betchay.
- Yes?

512
00:21:42,067 --> 00:21:43,233
Why don't you prepare some food?

513
00:21:43,233 --> 00:21:45,767
- Yeah, we've got dried fish!
- Gabo must be starving.

514
00:21:45,767 --> 00:21:47,600
- Come on, son.
- Come on, let's eat.

515
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:48,700
[GABO] Let's go.

516
00:21:49,867 --> 00:21:51,267
Can you believe
he's already out?

517
00:21:51,267 --> 00:21:52,800
[TEKLA] Let's eat!

518
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:54,633
- There, son.
- Sit over there.

519
00:21:54,633 --> 00:21:55,967
- [TEKLA] Can I join?
- Sure.

520
00:21:55,967 --> 00:21:57,933
[MAMENG] Come on in.

521
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:00,967
- Is it okay?
- Have a seat.

522
00:22:00,967 --> 00:22:03,067
- Thank you.
- Come on, let's eat.

523
00:22:03,067 --> 00:22:05,567
Pa, I brought food too.

524
00:22:05,933 --> 00:22:08,067
I bought it from the corner.
I've missed this.

525
00:22:08,067 --> 00:22:09,233
<i> - Pagpag?
</i>- Yes!

526
00:22:09,233 --> 00:22:10,967
It's been so long
since I've had it.

527
00:22:10,967 --> 00:22:13,133
[BETCHAY] Give it to me.
I'll put it on a plate.

528
00:22:13,133 --> 00:22:14,300
Really?

529
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:16,067
- Yeah.
- Up until now?

530
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:18,067
- That's still your favorite?
- Of course.

531
00:22:18,067 --> 00:22:19,900
We all grew up eating that,
didn't we?

532
00:22:19,900 --> 00:22:21,333
- Here you go.
- That's true.

533
00:22:21,333 --> 00:22:23,233
I still remember how
we'd pick the pieces

534
00:22:23,233 --> 00:22:25,000
- with the fewest bite marks.
- Right?

535
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,667
- Exactly.
- Go ahead, take some.

536
00:22:26,667 --> 00:22:29,000
And it's from all kinds
of different restaurants.

537
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,967
That's why it's special!

538
00:22:30,967 --> 00:22:32,700
- [LAUGHS]
- Mmm. Delicious!

539
00:22:33,567 --> 00:22:35,033
[DELGADO] Please distribute.

540
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:43,000
The files I'm giving you now
contain your next case.

541
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,600
Large-scale illegal gold mining.

542
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,867
They're mining gold

543
00:22:47,067 --> 00:22:51,667
and supplying it to
major jewelers in Chinatown.

544
00:22:51,700 --> 00:22:54,333
We've also learned that
they're distributing it

545
00:22:54,333 --> 00:22:56,833
to different countries
across Southeast Asia.

546
00:22:56,833 --> 00:23:01,133
This is a major syndicate
with worldwide connections.

547
00:23:01,133 --> 00:23:04,833
That's why we need to find out
who's behind it,

548
00:23:05,667 --> 00:23:07,633
put a stop to their operations,

549
00:23:07,633 --> 00:23:09,667
and hold them accountable
under the law.

550
00:23:11,033 --> 00:23:13,600
And, uh, Head Agent Jacinto,

551
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,600
you'll be leading
this investigation.

552
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:17,833
It's time for you to step up.

553
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:21,067
- Sir, me?
- Yes.

554
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:23,067
I have great confidence in you,

555
00:23:23,067 --> 00:23:25,367
which is why I'm entrusting
this major case to you.

556
00:23:25,867 --> 00:23:27,200
You can do this.

557
00:23:28,367 --> 00:23:30,267
We're right behind you, Ma'am.

558
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:33,367
I'll need all of your help.

559
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:39,033
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

560
00:23:39,367 --> 00:23:44,233
[DELGADO] This is your
first case as team leader.

561
00:23:44,233 --> 00:23:45,967
How do you feel?

562
00:23:45,967 --> 00:23:48,067
I'm ready to take on
the challenge, Sir.

563
00:23:48,067 --> 00:23:52,900
Your father was a
former general in the NLEA.

564
00:23:52,900 --> 00:23:57,033
I'm sure that's a heavy
responsibility to carry.

565
00:23:57,700 --> 00:24:01,033
Honestly, Sir, I am nervous.

566
00:24:01,767 --> 00:24:03,700
I don't even know
why you entrusted me

567
00:24:03,700 --> 00:24:04,900
to lead the team.

568
00:24:04,900 --> 00:24:07,133
Why would you doubt yourself?

569
00:24:07,767 --> 00:24:10,100
The Zaragoza
Robbery Group case

570
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:12,100
and all the cases before that,

571
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:14,200
none of those criminals
would've been caught

572
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,733
without your skills.

573
00:24:15,733 --> 00:24:18,833
Aside from being capable,
you have a good heart.

574
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:22,367
And if that's what guides you,

575
00:24:22,367 --> 00:24:24,367
I'm sure you'll succeed.

576
00:24:26,433 --> 00:24:27,900
Thank you very much, Sir.

577
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:29,733
Jacinto.

578
00:24:30,367 --> 00:24:34,667
Don't doubt yourself.

579
00:24:35,233 --> 00:24:37,767
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

580
00:24:39,733 --> 00:24:41,033
- Hey, have some rice!
- Take some more.

581
00:24:41,033 --> 00:24:42,867
[DANTE] I hope you've learned
your lesson, Gabo.

582
00:24:42,867 --> 00:24:44,467
Be good from now on.

583
00:24:44,467 --> 00:24:45,867
- Hey.
- What?

584
00:24:45,867 --> 00:24:49,367
My nephew's always been
a good kid.

585
00:24:50,133 --> 00:24:52,867
They're the ones
who keep picking on him.

586
00:24:52,867 --> 00:24:54,067
Oh, that's true.

587
00:24:54,067 --> 00:24:56,133
Gabo's not really
the troublemaker here.

588
00:24:56,133 --> 00:24:57,200
They're the ones.

589
00:24:57,200 --> 00:25:00,267
Especially Django's
and Mister Paquito's gang.

590
00:25:00,267 --> 00:25:01,667
Exactly.

591
00:25:02,267 --> 00:25:03,567
[BONG] That's true, Gabo.

592
00:25:03,933 --> 00:25:05,733
Ever since you left,

593
00:25:05,733 --> 00:25:07,333
Paquito and his gang...

594
00:25:07,333 --> 00:25:10,700
...have been running
all the crime around here.

595
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,300
You know why?

596
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:17,333
Even the robbers,
snatchers, and scammers...

597
00:25:17,333 --> 00:25:18,800
...are hiding out with us.

598
00:25:19,333 --> 00:25:21,267
Why don't the cops arrest them?

599
00:25:21,267 --> 00:25:22,400
How can they?

600
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:24,033
The cops are the ones
protecting them.

601
00:25:25,167 --> 00:25:28,167
[RUDY] That's why you need
to be careful, Gabo.

602
00:25:28,167 --> 00:25:30,167
It's dangerous
for outsiders here now.

603
00:25:30,167 --> 00:25:32,600
Especially now that
Paquito's gang is growing.

604
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:36,733
Why should I be
careful around them, Pa?

605
00:25:38,033 --> 00:25:40,167
Django's the reason
I ended up in prison.

606
00:25:40,167 --> 00:25:42,100
I rotted in there
for eight years.

607
00:25:43,767 --> 00:25:46,000
He better hide
when we cross paths.

608
00:25:47,267 --> 00:25:48,967
[BETCHAY] Hey, Gabo.

609
00:25:48,967 --> 00:25:50,267
Don't say that.

610
00:25:50,267 --> 00:25:53,367
Stop getting
into fights already.

611
00:25:53,367 --> 00:25:55,667
That's why
you keep getting hurt.

612
00:25:55,667 --> 00:25:58,633
Straighten yourself out.
Learn your lesson.

613
00:25:58,633 --> 00:26:01,033
Let's change the subject.

614
00:26:01,033 --> 00:26:01,933
Wait a second.

615
00:26:01,933 --> 00:26:03,367
Why didn't you
tell us you were coming?

616
00:26:03,367 --> 00:26:05,033
- We would've picked you up.
- Exactly!

617
00:26:05,033 --> 00:26:06,667
- What was that about?
- Right! Mh-mm.

618
00:26:07,333 --> 00:26:08,400
Uh...

619
00:26:09,033 --> 00:26:10,267
It all happened so suddenly, Pa.

620
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:14,933
I didn't expect
to get released so soon.

621
00:26:15,233 --> 00:26:16,667
I was granted parole.

622
00:26:17,133 --> 00:26:18,400
They granted you parole?

623
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,867
[MAMENG] That's great.

624
00:26:20,867 --> 00:26:22,733
- [GABO] Uhm, auntie...
- [MAMENG] Hmm?

625
00:26:22,733 --> 00:26:25,067
I really behaved
while I was in prison.

626
00:26:25,067 --> 00:26:27,667
I did everything
they told me to do.

627
00:26:27,667 --> 00:26:30,967
So even though I still had
a long sentence left,

628
00:26:30,967 --> 00:26:33,033
they granted me parole
and released me early.

629
00:26:33,033 --> 00:26:34,800
- Oh, wow.
- That's great.

630
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:36,300
- So that's how it works.
- That's nice.

631
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:38,367
- Just behave in prison.
- So that's possible.

632
00:26:40,233 --> 00:26:41,200
Show me.

633
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:43,133
Here, sir.

634
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:46,767
[MAN] Sir! Sir!

635
00:26:46,767 --> 00:26:48,200
So many illegal
connections here!

636
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:49,933
There's so much wiring here!

637
00:26:49,933 --> 00:26:51,333
These people are unbelievable!

638
00:26:51,333 --> 00:26:53,267
Always stealing electricity!

639
00:26:53,267 --> 00:26:54,867
Go ahead. Cut them.

640
00:26:54,867 --> 00:26:58,167
As long as they don't learn,

641
00:26:58,167 --> 00:27:00,233
they'll never stop
using illegal connections.

642
00:27:00,233 --> 00:27:01,433
Yes, sir. Let's go.

643
00:27:01,433 --> 00:27:03,700
They won't stop
stealing electricity

644
00:27:03,700 --> 00:27:05,867
- until those wires catch fire.
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

645
00:27:05,867 --> 00:27:08,067
You hear me?
That's theft!

646
00:27:08,067 --> 00:27:09,233
It's illegal!

647
00:27:09,233 --> 00:27:10,433
[PEOPLE COMPLAINING]

648
00:27:10,433 --> 00:27:11,700
It's illegal!

649
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:14,433
[PEOPLE COMPLAINING]

650
00:27:14,433 --> 00:27:16,933
If those wires catch fire,

651
00:27:16,967 --> 00:27:20,200
all your houses
will burn down!

652
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:24,267
[PEOPLE COMPLAINING]

653
00:27:24,267 --> 00:27:25,867
[FAN STOPS]

654
00:27:26,233 --> 00:27:27,433
[HAIR CLIPPER BUZZING STOPS]

655
00:27:27,967 --> 00:27:28,767
[POWER CUTS OFF]

656
00:27:28,767 --> 00:27:30,733
- What happened?
- Power outage?

657
00:27:30,733 --> 00:27:32,333
Go check
what's happening outside.

658
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:37,367
[MAN] You'll all burn!
Remember that!

659
00:27:37,367 --> 00:27:38,533
It's illegal!

660
00:27:38,533 --> 00:27:40,100
[PEOPLE COMPLAINING]

661
00:27:40,100 --> 00:27:41,367
Remember that!

662
00:27:41,867 --> 00:27:43,833
It's the Manelco.
Tell Mister Rudy what happened.

663
00:27:44,133 --> 00:27:46,767
- This is exciting.
- [MAN] Yes! You never learn!

664
00:27:48,267 --> 00:27:49,867
- Mister Rudy!
- Oh?

665
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:51,333
Our favorite visitors are here.

666
00:27:51,333 --> 00:27:52,567
The Manelco is here.

667
00:27:52,567 --> 00:27:54,400
They cutting us off again.

668
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:56,400
They've got some nerve.

669
00:27:56,400 --> 00:28:00,100
How dare they cut off
our electricity

670
00:28:00,100 --> 00:28:02,867
when we're paying so much!

671
00:28:03,467 --> 00:28:05,333
- Hey! What now?!
- Oh no, there she is.

672
00:28:05,333 --> 00:28:06,967
There she is! This is exciting.

673
00:28:06,967 --> 00:28:10,900
Someone's losing it again!

674
00:28:10,900 --> 00:28:14,233
You'll all burn!
You can't reconnect those!

675
00:28:14,233 --> 00:28:15,767
[PEOPLE COMPLAINING]

676
00:28:15,767 --> 00:28:16,800
Do you understand?

677
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:19,067
Listen to this guy!

678
00:28:19,067 --> 00:28:20,400
Because you keep
doing it over and over!

679
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:21,433
Illegal connections!

680
00:28:21,433 --> 00:28:22,833
What do you want?

681
00:28:22,867 --> 00:28:24,433
You want us to pay?

682
00:28:24,433 --> 00:28:26,267
You're charging way too much!

683
00:28:26,267 --> 00:28:27,833
- That's right!
- That's right!

684
00:28:27,833 --> 00:28:30,433
[BETCHAY] You keep adding
all kinds of charges!

685
00:28:30,433 --> 00:28:33,433
It's so expensive!
Charges here, charges there!

686
00:28:33,433 --> 00:28:37,467
And do you know why the
Philippines isn't progressing?

687
00:28:37,467 --> 00:28:40,933
Because you keep robbing us
poor people!

688
00:28:40,933 --> 00:28:42,133
- That's right!
- That's right!

689
00:28:42,133 --> 00:28:45,167
What? You want us to play fair?

690
00:28:45,167 --> 00:28:46,967
You're the ones
taking advantage of us!

691
00:28:46,967 --> 00:28:48,500
You want us
to pay the right amount?

692
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:50,800
Then are your charges fair?

693
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:51,833
- That's right!
- Hey, Rudy.

694
00:28:51,833 --> 00:28:55,200
Rudy, you know that's illegal.
You're stealing!

695
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:56,833
I can have you arrested!

696
00:28:56,867 --> 00:28:59,000
- Hey!
- Hey!

697
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:00,533
[BETCHAY]
Who are you arresting?!

698
00:29:00,533 --> 00:29:01,867
Go ahead. Try it!

699
00:29:01,867 --> 00:29:05,300
[PEOPLE COMPLAINING]

700
00:29:05,300 --> 00:29:07,467
Yes, what we're doing
may be wrong,

701
00:29:07,467 --> 00:29:08,833
I'll have you all arrested!

702
00:29:08,833 --> 00:29:10,233
but I hope those in power
also think about

703
00:29:10,233 --> 00:29:11,500
what we're going through.

704
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:18,467
[OVERLAPPING VOICES COMPLAINING]

705
00:29:21,567 --> 00:29:25,133
Even if they keep
cutting off our power,

706
00:29:25,133 --> 00:29:26,367
they'll just tire
themselves out!

707
00:29:26,367 --> 00:29:27,333
- That's right!
- That's right!

708
00:29:27,333 --> 00:29:29,367
- Get lost!
- Tule!

709
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:30,533
Go climb it already!

710
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:38,533
- Tule! Tule! Tule!
- Tule! Tule! Tule!

711
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:45,867
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

712
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:47,433
Neighbors!

713
00:29:47,433 --> 00:29:49,100
The power's back!

714
00:29:49,100 --> 00:29:50,500
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

715
00:29:50,500 --> 00:29:52,233
Hey! Hey!
What are we waiting for?

716
00:29:52,233 --> 00:29:55,200
Neighbors! Let's celebrate!

717
00:29:55,200 --> 00:30:01,900
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

718
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:05,567
Unlimited power again!
Blast all your air conditioners!

719
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:08,567
Turn on every TV,
even if nobody's watching!

720
00:30:08,567 --> 00:30:10,267
- Yes!
- Let's enjoy it!

721
00:30:10,267 --> 00:30:17,233
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

722
00:30:20,100 --> 00:30:21,567
[WOMAN] Let's all buy
air conditioners!

723
00:30:21,567 --> 00:30:28,533
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

724
00:30:30,367 --> 00:30:31,967
- [PAQUITO] Django.
- Pa?

725
00:30:31,967 --> 00:30:34,100
You're in charge here
while I'm gone.

726
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:37,167
Make sure
the business runs smoothly.

727
00:30:37,933 --> 00:30:39,467
If anything comes up,

728
00:30:40,067 --> 00:30:41,267
just give me a call.

729
00:30:41,267 --> 00:30:43,500
Don't worry
about things here, Pa.

730
00:30:43,500 --> 00:30:44,933
I'll handle everything.

731
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:46,500
Okay.

732
00:30:46,500 --> 00:30:48,000
- Hmm.
- Oh?

733
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,967
Take care.
Take care, all of you.

734
00:30:49,967 --> 00:30:51,433
[CHUCKLES WRYLY]

735
00:30:51,433 --> 00:30:53,433
- They better be.
- [LAUGHS]

736
00:30:53,433 --> 00:30:54,933
- Whatever.
- Oh...

737
00:30:54,933 --> 00:30:56,167
- Where's my kiss?
- [SMOOCHES]

738
00:30:56,167 --> 00:30:57,467
Oh, wow!

739
00:30:57,467 --> 00:30:59,167
- Take care.
- Okay.

740
00:30:59,167 --> 00:31:02,733
[HEAVY BEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

741
00:31:02,733 --> 00:31:04,300
- There!
- [TOLITS] Django!

742
00:31:04,300 --> 00:31:06,033
- Django! Django! Django!
- Hurry up.

743
00:31:07,933 --> 00:31:08,900
[DABOY] Django!

744
00:31:10,667 --> 00:31:11,667
Hey!

745
00:31:12,267 --> 00:31:15,000
You three! Where's your take?

746
00:31:15,967 --> 00:31:18,233
[DABOY] Sorry, Django.
We couldn't pull anything off.

747
00:31:18,600 --> 00:31:19,967
- [BLOW LANDS]
- Ouch, Django!

748
00:31:19,967 --> 00:31:21,433
You idiots!

749
00:31:21,433 --> 00:31:25,667
Even the kids
have already hit their quota!

750
00:31:25,667 --> 00:31:28,133
You haven't even
given me a single peso!

751
00:31:28,133 --> 00:31:30,667
Things were really slow, Django.

752
00:31:31,333 --> 00:31:33,100
We promise
we'll make up for it.

753
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:34,100
- [BLOW LANDS]
- Ouch!

754
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:35,500
- [THUD]
- [GRUNTS, GASPS]

755
00:31:36,167 --> 00:31:37,600
Is that so?!

756
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:40,633
You useless losers!

757
00:31:40,633 --> 00:31:42,433
Sorry, Django.

758
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:45,367
We promise we'll hit
our quota next time.

759
00:31:45,367 --> 00:31:46,467
Sorry?

760
00:31:46,467 --> 00:31:48,500
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GROANS]

761
00:31:50,333 --> 00:31:52,500
Wasn't our rule...

762
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:55,433
...that nobody comes back
to headquarters empty-handed?

763
00:31:56,300 --> 00:31:57,300
- [SLAPS]
- [GRUNTS]

764
00:31:57,300 --> 00:31:58,733
- Ouch!
- That hurts.

765
00:31:58,733 --> 00:32:00,367
Why are you here?!

766
00:32:00,367 --> 00:32:01,700
We were supposed
to tell you something,

767
00:32:01,700 --> 00:32:04,400
but you kept slapping us.
How can we even say it?

768
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:06,000
- Oh, no!
- Don't get sarcastic with me!

769
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:07,667
- What is it?!
- It's important.

770
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:11,000
It's Gabo.

771
00:32:11,333 --> 00:32:13,000
We saw him here.

772
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,700
He's out.
He went home.

773
00:32:14,700 --> 00:32:16,000
G-Gabo?

774
00:32:16,567 --> 00:32:17,833
Wasn't he supposed
to have years left?

775
00:32:17,833 --> 00:32:19,033
How'd he get out?

776
00:32:19,033 --> 00:32:20,367
We don't know.

777
00:32:20,367 --> 00:32:22,400
[PEPE] Hey, Django, this is bad.

778
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:25,167
After all those years in prison,
he'll definitely come after you.

779
00:32:25,167 --> 00:32:29,367
Django, let's call your father
and have him come back.

780
00:32:29,367 --> 00:32:30,367
No.

781
00:32:31,167 --> 00:32:32,500
Don't tell my father.

782
00:32:33,700 --> 00:32:35,367
I'll deal with Gabo myself.

783
00:32:36,100 --> 00:32:37,400
- Pulgas!
- Oh?

784
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:39,133
- Hurry up!
- Why?

785
00:32:40,067 --> 00:32:41,400
Go find Gabo.

786
00:32:42,667 --> 00:32:44,033
Tell him...

787
00:32:45,033 --> 00:32:46,800
...to meet me
at the headquarters.

788
00:32:48,100 --> 00:32:49,633
If he wants revenge,

789
00:32:50,733 --> 00:32:52,500
we'll settle it here.

790
00:32:53,367 --> 00:32:54,567
Tell him...

791
00:32:54,567 --> 00:32:57,067
I'll make sure he's the one
they mourn

792
00:32:57,067 --> 00:32:58,500
here in Ginintuang Lupa.

793
00:32:59,067 --> 00:33:00,500
- Quick!
- Yes, boss! Come on!

794
00:33:00,867 --> 00:33:02,133
Hurry up!

795
00:33:02,133 --> 00:33:09,067
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

796
00:33:12,433 --> 00:33:13,567
[TEKLA] So, did you
miss it here, Gabo?

797
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:16,367
Miss Diday was fuming earlier.

798
00:33:16,367 --> 00:33:19,200
And now, Manelco cut off
our electricity.

799
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:20,267
- Wow!
- [CHUCKLING]

800
00:33:20,267 --> 00:33:22,200
It seems like we've given you
a warm welcome.

801
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:23,567
[BETCHAY] I think
it's the opposite.

802
00:33:23,900 --> 00:33:27,900
Your arrival seems to be
a bad omen, isn't it?

803
00:33:27,900 --> 00:33:30,733
[BETCHAY] I think before
you came here,

804
00:33:30,733 --> 00:33:33,567
you should've gone someplace
else first to lose bad luck.

805
00:33:33,567 --> 00:33:35,733
Look at this woman.

806
00:33:35,733 --> 00:33:37,900
Aren't you happy
that Gabo's here?

807
00:33:37,900 --> 00:33:40,733
[MAMENG] He has a chance
to start anew here.

808
00:33:40,733 --> 00:33:42,400
Did I say I wasn't happy
about his return?

809
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:43,900
- I'm just saying that--
- No, what you're--

810
00:33:43,900 --> 00:33:45,233
Wait a second!

811
00:33:45,233 --> 00:33:47,233
My son has behaved now, okay?

812
00:33:47,233 --> 00:33:49,233
He'll turn over a new leaf.
Won't you, son?

813
00:33:49,233 --> 00:33:51,200
- Right?
- Really?

814
00:33:52,233 --> 00:33:53,600
- Yes, Dad.
- See that?

815
00:33:53,600 --> 00:33:54,767
- See?
- You didn't believe him.

816
00:33:54,767 --> 00:33:57,400
I didn't say that
he wouldn't change!

817
00:33:57,433 --> 00:34:01,267
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

818
00:34:01,267 --> 00:34:03,233
- Gabo!
- Aren't those Django's boys?

819
00:34:03,867 --> 00:34:06,467
Hey, Gabo!
Django is asking for you.

820
00:34:06,467 --> 00:34:07,467
What did he say?

821
00:34:07,467 --> 00:34:08,633
If you're really brave,

822
00:34:08,633 --> 00:34:11,300
you should face Django
at the stables.

823
00:34:11,300 --> 00:34:14,467
That will let people know who's
the bigger man between you.

824
00:34:14,467 --> 00:34:16,633
- Bigger man?
- Why is that needed?

825
00:34:16,633 --> 00:34:18,267
Don't you agree to
his challenge, okay?

826
00:34:18,267 --> 00:34:20,300
Get out of here!
Get out of here!

827
00:34:20,300 --> 00:34:21,600
- Go away!
- Get out of here!

828
00:34:21,600 --> 00:34:23,300
You just got out of jail, Gabo.
You had just gotten freed!

829
00:34:23,300 --> 00:34:25,700
Gabo, let me tell you this.

830
00:34:25,700 --> 00:34:28,867
[BONG] Django will not stop
until he gets back at you.

831
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:30,500
[IPE] What can we say?

832
00:34:30,500 --> 00:34:33,500
Django got humiliated
in their last fight.

833
00:34:33,500 --> 00:34:36,467
He will never stop until
he takes revenge on you.

834
00:34:36,467 --> 00:34:39,433
Gabo, don't listen to Ipe.

835
00:34:39,800 --> 00:34:42,633
Besides, Gabo, you won't
be able to do anything

836
00:34:42,633 --> 00:34:44,467
if you take on
Django's challenge.

837
00:34:44,467 --> 00:34:47,300
You're already free. Don't let
yourself go back to jail.

838
00:34:47,300 --> 00:34:49,700
[MAMENG] Or worse,
you could be killed.

839
00:34:49,700 --> 00:34:51,300
[BETCHAY] What, Gabo?

840
00:34:51,867 --> 00:34:55,433
Will you prove to us that
you have changed your ways now?

841
00:34:57,233 --> 00:35:00,200
Gabo, you changed already,
haven't you?

842
00:35:00,700 --> 00:35:02,700
Aren't you going to be nice now?

843
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:09,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

844
00:35:09,733 --> 00:35:11,733
That's great.

845
00:35:11,733 --> 00:35:13,733
[BETCHAY SCOFFS] Really?

846
00:35:13,733 --> 00:35:15,333
[RUDY] You have no trust in him.

847
00:35:15,333 --> 00:35:18,467
[TEKLA] Do you really believe
that he's changed?

848
00:35:23,867 --> 00:35:25,167
See?

849
00:35:25,167 --> 00:35:27,233
You know, I'm delighted
to see Gabo like that.

850
00:35:27,233 --> 00:35:28,567
He has really changed.

851
00:35:28,567 --> 00:35:30,567
- [SCOFFS] Oh?
- You're delighted?

852
00:35:30,567 --> 00:35:32,533
Aren't you wondering
if that's still Gabo?

853
00:35:32,533 --> 00:35:34,700
That man's too different
from the Gabo we know.

854
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:36,533
Do you really think Gabo will
back down from Django?

855
00:35:36,567 --> 00:35:38,567
- Think about it!
- [IPE] You saw it yourself.

856
00:35:38,567 --> 00:35:40,567
He just left peacefully.

857
00:35:40,567 --> 00:35:42,400
He wasn't looking for a fight.
He didn't bite back.

858
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:45,400
- That's right!
- The rumors are true.

859
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:48,400
I'm going to bet my life on it.

860
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:50,400
My son is turning
over a new leaf.

861
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:51,567
- [BONG] Okay.
- [IPE] I agree with you.

862
00:35:51,567 --> 00:35:53,233
I'll make a bet against yours.

863
00:35:53,233 --> 00:35:55,233
- Okay, call.
- Let's see.

864
00:35:55,233 --> 00:35:57,400
- [DOOR CRASHES]
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING]

865
00:35:57,400 --> 00:35:59,800
- Gabo!
- Let him face me!

866
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,800
- [SCREAMING CONTINUES]
- [POOL THUDS]

867
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:04,800
- Gabo! Stop!
- Where is he?!

868
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:07,400
- Huh? Where is he?!
- Gabo!

869
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:09,600
- Stop him!
- Gabo!

870
00:36:10,333 --> 00:36:11,300
Where is he?!

871
00:36:11,300 --> 00:36:12,467
- What are we going to do?
- Get our stuff!

872
00:36:12,467 --> 00:36:15,267
- This will be chaotic!
- Come on, hurry!

873
00:36:15,267 --> 00:36:17,667
- Gabo!
- Where is he going?

874
00:36:17,667 --> 00:36:19,833
Come on, we need to hurry!

875
00:36:19,833 --> 00:36:20,767
We need to go!

876
00:36:20,767 --> 00:36:22,667
- Where is Django hiding?
- We don't know!

877
00:36:22,667 --> 00:36:23,800
- [BLADE SWISHES]
- Those are kids!

878
00:36:23,800 --> 00:36:25,800
You're in danger now, Django!

879
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:27,800
[PEOPLE SHOUTING]

880
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:29,967
Where's Django? Where is he?

881
00:36:29,967 --> 00:36:32,333
[SHOUTING CONTINUES]

882
00:36:32,333 --> 00:36:34,700
Where's Django?! Where is he?!

883
00:36:35,500 --> 00:36:36,433
Django!

884
00:36:36,900 --> 00:36:38,700
Come on, let's go!

885
00:36:39,300 --> 00:36:42,167
<i>Your Aunt Pinky has this piece
of property that we bought.</i>

886
00:36:42,167 --> 00:36:43,167
<i> Where is it located?</i>

887
00:36:43,200 --> 00:36:44,833
<i> In Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

888
00:36:44,833 --> 00:36:46,200
<i>Aren't there a lot of
families there?</i>

889
00:36:46,200 --> 00:36:48,200
<i>The people there are known
to be criminals too.</i>

890
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:55,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

891
00:36:58,367 --> 00:37:00,533
<i> This will be your end!</i>

892
00:37:00,533 --> 00:37:04,133
[MALE VO] Gabo and Django
will clash once again.

893
00:37:04,133 --> 00:37:05,933
<i> Gabo!</i>

894
00:37:08,533 --> 00:37:13,800
[MALE VO] The real gangster
will be revealed now.

895
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:16,200
<i>You're the reason why
I was in jail for eight years!</i>

896
00:37:16,200 --> 00:37:18,367
You're going to pay for it all!

897
00:37:18,400 --> 00:37:21,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

898
00:37:21,367 --> 00:37:22,867
[MALE VO] Coco Martin's Sigabo.
